"""Build the evaluation report from saved counts; no model execution."""
import csv,json
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent/'checkpoints/baseline-5epochs/evaluation'
with (p/'per_class_metrics.csv').open() as f: classes=list(csv.DictReader(f))
with (p/'confusion_pairs_by_count.csv').open() as f: counts=list(csv.DictReader(f))
with (p/'confusion_pairs_by_rate.csv').open() as f: rates=list(csv.DictReader(f))
with (p/'qualitative_selection.csv').open() as f: examples=list(csv.DictReader(f))
m=json.loads((p/'metrics.json').read_text())
worst=sorted(classes,key=lambda r:float(r['iou']))
lines=['# Epoch-19 Fast-SCNN evaluation','','I evaluated the unchanged best.keras checkpoint on all 500 Cityscapes validation images.','No training occurred and no weights, architecture, labels, optimizer state or training settings were changed.','','## Overall results','','| Metric | Recomputed | Epoch-19 history |','|---|---:|---:|',
'| Pixel Accuracy | 88.669757% | 88.670235% |','| mIoU | 0.422975283 | 0.422977000 |','| Macro Dice | 0.540340069 | 0.540338448 |','| Validation loss | 0.341819176 | 0.341814935 |','',
'I counted 228,972,480 valid pixels and excluded 33,171,520 void pixels after resizing.','All class support counts below refer to valid pixels at 512 x 1024, not original-resolution pixels or object instances.','The largest absolute discrepancy from the saved history is below 0.000005, consistent with small numerical differences in execution.','The evaluation loop took 28.83 seconds; the initial script, including loading, checks and artifact generation, took 50.71 seconds.','Later visual-layout correction and report writing are excluded from those timings.','These timings are not a real-time camera latency benchmark.','','## Checkpoint and method','','The model loaded with input shape (None, 512, 1024, 3), output shape (None, 512, 1024, 19), and 1,160,707 parameters.','Its optimizer iteration count remained 56,525, matching epoch 19.','All model weights, including BatchNorm moving statistics, and all optimizer variables were compared before and after and were unchanged.','The checkpoint SHA-256 before and after was '+m['sha256_before']+'.','Inference used GPU:0 and explicitly called model(images, training=False), with batch size 1.','I used the existing image normalization and nearest-neighbor mask resize.','Void ID 255 was excluded with the loader\'s zero sample weights, not counted as road or as a twentieth class.','The confusion matrix uses true classes as rows and predictions as columns, with integer counts accumulated across all images.','IoU is TP/(TP+FP+FN); Dice is 2TP/(2TP+FP+FN).','Both macro metrics average the 19 class scores after global accumulation; all 19 classes have nonzero support here.','Pixel Accuracy is the fraction of valid pixels classified correctly.','The loss uses the saved SparseCategoricalCrossentropy(from_logits=True) and its original sum_over_batch_size reduction.','Void pixels contribute zero loss but remain in its denominator, preserving comparability with training history.','I independently checked the global IoU/Dice calculation against the registered Keras metrics.','This is local validation at the requested resized resolution, not an official Cityscapes test-server benchmark result.','','## Per-class metrics by train ID','']
def table(records):
    result=['| ID | Class | IoU % | Dice % | Support pixels | Recall % |','|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for r in records:
        result.append(f"| {r['class_id']} | {r['class_name']} | {100*float(r['iou']):.2f} | {100*float(r['dice']):.2f} | {int(r['support_pixels']):,} | {100*float(r['recall']):.2f} |")
    return result
lines+=table(classes)
lines+=['','Recall here is pixel recall, not object-detection recall.','','## Per-class metrics from worst to best IoU','']+table(worst)
lines+=['','The strongest five classes are road, vegetation, sky, car and building.','The weakest five are train, motorcycle, rider, traffic light and truck.','The strongest five occupy approximately 86.76% of valid validation pixels; overall accuracy therefore hides weak performance on smaller classes.','Train appears in only 22 validation images and motorcycle in 93, so their low support also limits how broadly this validation result can be generalized.','Pole appears in 491 images and traffic sign in 473, yet their scores remain weak, indicating that rarity alone does not explain the failures.','','## Confusion analysis','','Row normalization expresses the percentage of each true class assigned to each predicted class.','The full diagonal is recall, not IoU.','Both raw counts and row-normalized data are saved.','','Largest wrong pairs by absolute pixel count:','','| True -> predicted | Pixels | % of true-class pixels |','|---|---:|---:|']
for r in counts[:10]: lines.append(f"| {r['true_class']} -> {r['predicted_class']} | {int(r['pixels']):,} | {float(r['percent_of_true_class']):.2f}% |")
lines+=['','Largest wrong pairs relative to their source class:','','| True -> predicted | Pixels | % of true-class pixels |','|---|---:|---:|']
for r in rates[:10]: lines.append(f"| {r['true_class']} -> {r['predicted_class']} | {int(r['pixels']):,} | {float(r['percent_of_true_class']):.2f}% |")
lines+=['','Sidewalk -> road is especially important: 2,069,017 pixels, or 16.71% of true sidewalk pixels.','The reverse road -> sidewalk rate is only 1.69%, illustrating why directional normalization matters.','Rider -> person is 30.95%; motorcycle -> car is 30.04% and motorcycle -> bicycle is 29.90%.','Wall -> building accounts for 17.58% of wall pixels.','Person -> building accounts for 16.39% of person pixels.','These are measured outcomes, not assumed confusion patterns.','','![Row-normalized confusion matrix](confusion_matrix.png)','','## PathClear-relevant interpretation','','I describe relative strengths within this validation set, not operational reliability for mobility assistance.','','- Road and car are the strongest mobility-related classes at 94.16% and 81.21% IoU.','- Sidewalk is moderate at 60.79% IoU, with 73.30% pixel recall and substantial leakage into road.','- Terrain is weak at 38.30% IoU; about 20.12% of its pixels become vegetation and 19.65% become sidewalk.','- Person and bicycle reach only 40.52% and 42.42% IoU, with pixel recall of 54.56% and 65.85%; partial or missed regions remain common.','- Rider and motorcycle are very weak at 15.64% and 7.80% IoU, with pixel recall of 23.65% and 11.15%.','- Bus and truck are weak at 34.57% and 18.26% IoU; vehicle-type confusion is substantial even though car is strong.','- Traffic sign, pole and traffic light are weak at 35.72%, 26.70% and 17.15% IoU.','- Only 18.49% of traffic-light pixels are correctly labelled; 42.79% become building and 30.52% become vegetation.','','I would not use these outputs alone to declare a path safe or an obstacle absent.','Cityscapes road/sidewalk semantics do not directly measure walkability, obstacle clearance or PathClear navigation capability.','This evaluation does not quantify object-instance detection, distance estimation, temporal consistency, occlusion-specific recall or real-world safety.','','## Qualitative inspection','','I saved twelve examples, each with original RGB, ground truth, prediction and a valid-pixel error map.','Red indicates wrong valid pixels, gray correct valid pixels and black ignored pixels.','Nine images are fixed quantiles of per-image mIoU: 5/10/15%, 45/50/55%, and 85/90/95%.','Three additional images explicitly target the weakest person, rider and motorcycle IoU among images with at least 200 true pixels of that class, excluding already selected examples.','This selection is intentionally balanced for diagnosis, not a random sample or an estimate of failure frequency.','Per-image mIoU averages classes present in that image or prediction and is used only for ranking examples; it is not the reported global mIoU.','Strong means relatively strong for this model, not error-free.','','I inspected all twelve examples.','The weak pedestrian scene in example 2 retains the road but loses most people against the building and fragments the cyclist.','Example 1 shows severe wall/bicycle/vegetation confusion on a narrow paved street.','The middle examples show broad road/car regions but miss poles, traffic signs and parts of riders; example 5 confuses a terrain strip with sidewalk.','The strong examples retain broad road/sidewalk structure, but still have poor thin-object boundaries and fragmented distant people.','Example 10 misses small person regions despite a reasonable image-level score; example 11 nearly erases a rider between cars.','Example 12 loses the small motorcycle label and distorts pedestrian/island boundaries.','Several distant or partly occluded subjects are poorly preserved, but I did not compute an occlusion-stratified metric.','','| Example | Selection | Image mIoU | File |','|---:|---|---:|---|']
for r in examples: lines.append(f"| {r['example']} | {r['selection_reason']} | {float(r['image_miou']):.3f} | [Open]({r['file']}) |")
lines+=['','## Recommended next step, not implemented','','I would keep this checkpoint as the baseline and prioritize a controlled augmentation experiment before simply extending the unchanged run.','The model preserves large regions but loses small structures and has a widening train/validation gap from the earlier training history.','A first candidate is synchronized image/mask scale-and-crop and horizontal-flip augmentation, with nearest-neighbor handling for masks; image-only color variation can be assessed separately.','The model input size can remain 512 x 1024, so a resolution increase is not the first variable to change.','TensorFlow\'s [segmentation tutorial](https://www.tensorflow.org/tutorials/images/segmentation) demonstrates applying matching spatial augmentation to images and masks.','','I would then audit the training split\'s class distribution and test class-aware sampling or capped training-derived class weights as a separate experiment.','The rare vehicle and rider failures motivate that investigation, but validation support must not be substituted for training statistics when setting weights.','The poor pole and sign results despite frequent image presence also mean class weighting alone is unlikely to solve the problem.','I would compare class recall/IoU and sidewalk -> road errors, not only pixel accuracy.','','I would collect and annotate a separate PathClear dataset in parallel, keeping a held-out local test set.','Fine-tuning on it is the later route to testing the glasses viewpoint and Philippine environments; Cityscapes performance does not establish that transfer.','I would defer architecture changes, resolution changes and extra regularization until controlled augmentation/sampling evidence identifies what remains unresolved.','No next training change, fine-tuning or additional training was implemented.','','## Files created','','- metrics.json: overall scores, runtime, hashes, invariance checks and history deltas.','- per_class_metrics.csv and per_class_metrics_by_iou.csv: 19-class IoU, Dice, support, precision, recall and image counts.','- confusion_matrix.csv and confusion_matrix_normalized.csv: raw and normalized numerical matrices.','- confusion_matrix.png: normalized heatmap.','- confusion_pairs_by_count.csv and confusion_pairs_by_rate.csv: directional errors.','- per_image_metrics.csv: all 500 image scores.','- predictions/: 500 cached train-ID prediction masks.','- qualitative/: twelve four-panel comparisons.','- qualitative_selection.csv: exact source images and selection reasons.','- qualitative_gallery.md: full image gallery.','- evaluation_summary.md: this report.','- Repository helpers evaluate_baseline.py, render_evaluation.py and write_evaluation_report.py were added; existing training files were not edited.','- evaluation_run.log is stored in the parent baseline directory.','','Reference for the class-level metric: [Cityscapes benchmark suite](https://www.cityscapes-dataset.com/benchmarks/).']
(p/'evaluation_summary.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
gallery=['# Epoch-19 qualitative evaluation','','I selected nine score-stratified images and three targeted class failures; these are diagnostic examples, not a random sample.','']
for r in examples: gallery += [f"## Example {r['example']}",'',r['selection_reason']+'.','',f"![Example {r['example']}]({r['file']})",'']
(p/'qualitative_gallery.md').write_text('\n'.join(gallery),encoding='utf-8')
print('Saved evaluation_summary.md and qualitative_gallery.md.')
